The HGDB mandatory access control module
----------------------------------------

This directory contains the source code of MAC machenism.


Basically, This directory currently only contain mandatory access rules. 
Because some priviliges problem ,the functions to support other feature,
such as get/set seclabel, compare seclabels are moved to the /src directory. 
Maybe someday those functions will be moved back to make this extension easier
to maintain. 

The code in hg_hooks.c provide the function about table-level MAC rules.
In short, the table-level access rules will be like the pseudo code as 
following,

switch(query->commandType)
{
	case CMD_SELECT:
		if (!HgRowLevelSecurityIsON)
		{
			if(Compare_Two_Labels(sub_seclabel,obj_seclabel) == LABEL_UNCOMPARABLE)
				report error!!
		}
		else
		{
			if(relkind == RELKIND_RELATION)
				hg_make_rowlevel_quals_node(query,varno);
					
		}
		break;

	case CMD_UPDATE:
		if (Compare_Two_Labels(sub_seclabel,obj_seclabel) != LABEL_EQUAL)	
			report error!!
				
		if (HgRowLevelSecurityIsON)
			if(relkind == RELKIND_RELATION)
				hg_make_rowlevel_quals_node(query,varno);
					
		break;

	case CMD_DELETE:
		if (Compare_Two_Labels(sub_seclabel,obj_seclabel) != LABEL_EQUAL)
			report error!!
		if (HgRowLevelSecurityIsON)
			if(relkind == RELKIND_RELATION)
				hg_make_rowlevel_quals_node(query,varno);
	
		break;
			
	case CMD_INSERT:
		if (Compare_Two_Labels(obj_seclabel,sub_seclabel) == LABEL_UNCOMPARABLE)
			report error!!
		break;
			
	default:
		break;
}

And it also provide the function to link the extension with internal 
hooks. You can find more details in the decrisption above each function in 
the file.

The code in file row-level.c contain the functions to support row-level mandatory
access control rules. When enable row-level mandatory access control, the system will 
apply row-level check rules to the query by calling function hg_make_rowlevel_quals_node().
Funciton hg_make_rowlevel_quals_node() add a condition node to the query, just like add 
the access control rule as a WHERE clause in query.And more details can be found 
in each funciotn's decription.
